README.md
# vendor/android is excluded PER DIRECTORY rather than as `vendor/android` plus
# a `!vendor/android/tinyxml2` exception. The exception form does not work: the
# context builder prunes the excluded directory's subtree, so the negation
# re-included the directory entry and none of its contents, and the build died
# inside the container with
#
#     No rule to make target '/opt/library/vendor/android/tinyxml2/tinyxml2.cpp'
#
# Listing the five big ones by name has no such ambiguity, and tinyxml2 -- which
# the Debian library compiles in, see base.mk -- is simply never excluded.
# Sizes are why this list exists at all: these five are ~585 MB of Android SDL
# and glm sources that nothing in this image can build. tinyxml2 is 3.7 MB.
#
# ADD A LINE HERE IF A NEW ANDROID-ONLY SUBMODULE APPEARS. The old blanket
# pattern needed no maintenance; this one does.
vendor/android/SDL2
vendor/android/SDL_image2
vendor/android/SDL_mixer2
vendor/android/SDL_ttf2
vendor/android/glm
# Cross-compiled example trees. Dockerfile.debian copies examples/ so CI can
# build them, but these two need devkitPro and the Android NDK respectively —
# nothing in the image can compile them, and together they are ~200 MB of
# build context.
examples/nx-platformer
examples/android-platformer
